---
title: Library & culling
description: Open folders, sort by capture time, and cut a shoot down with picks, rejects and star ratings before you develop anything.
---

The Library sidebar is where a session starts. **Files…** opens individual photos, **Folder…**
opens a directory. Latent reads the folder as it finds it — your existing tree stays the
organising principle, and nothing is copied into a catalogue of its own.

Opened folders appear under **Folders** with a count beside each one, and nest as your directories
do. **Collections** are the one grouping Latent adds on top: a named set you assemble by hand,
for frames that belong together but do not live in the same directory.

## Culling

The point of the grid is to get from everything you shot down to the frames worth developing.
Three independent marks do that work:

- **Rating** — zero to five stars.
- **Pick** — the keeper flag.
- **Reject** — the opposite.

Pick and reject are separate from the star rating, so you can flag a frame as a keeper and still
rank it against the other keepers.

In the grid view the shortcuts are on the hint line at the bottom of the window:

- `0`–`5` — set the star rating
- `P` — pick
- `X` — reject
- arrow keys — move between frames
- `Enter` or double-click — open the selected frame for editing

The **Size** slider scales the grid thumbnails; **Done** returns you to the editing view.

## Filtering and sorting

Above the folder tree, the filter tabs narrow what you are looking at: **All**, **Picks**,
**Rejects**, and **3★+** for everything rated three stars or better. The search field matches on
filename and camera, and **Sort** orders the set — by capture time, so a shoot reads in the order
you took it, rather than in whatever order the filenames happen to fall.

## Grid and filmstrip

The filmstrip along the bottom keeps the whole set to hand while you work on one frame, and shows
each thumbnail's rating and flags. **Grid** switches to the full-window contact sheet for culling
in bulk. Both views share the same selection, filters and sort.
